### 4. Wire the new schema through the MCP server registration site

Read: `coding-playbook/api/validation`, `coding-playbook/foundations/conventions`

- [x] 4a. In `src/index.ts`, locate the `aide_brain` entry inside
      the `ListToolsRequestSchema` handler. Update its `inputSchema`
      from `{ type: "object", properties: {} }` to:
      ```
      {
        type: "object",
        properties: {
          kind: {
            type: "string",
            enum: ["orientation", "config"],
            description: "<one-line description of the two-value vocabulary, naming the default and what each value returns>",
          },
        },
      }
      ```
      The MCP framework validates against this inputSchema before
      the handler runs; an unknown value or wrong type fails at the
      framework boundary with a structured error, exactly as the
      spec's Strategy paragraph "Schema-level rejection of unknown
      `kind` values, not handler-level" requires. Do NOT add `kind`
      to a `required` array — it is optional.
- [x] 4b. Rewrite the registered `description` string for
      `aide_brain`. The new description must teach: (i) the optional
      `kind` parameter and its closed two-value vocabulary
      (`"orientation" | "config"`); (ii) the default
      (`"orientation"`); (iii) what each value returns (orientation
      = runtime briefing when an agent reaches for the brain
      mid-task; config = integration-specific wiring flow used by
      `/aide:brain config`); (iv) that install-time seed sections
      (`playbookIndex`, `studyPlaybook`, `updatePlaybook`,
      `researchIndex`) are NOT surfaced via this tool — agents
      reach those via the brain's read tool against the on-disk
      seed files; (v) the response shape is `{ status, instructions
      }` only — no `backend`, `connector`, or `name`; (vi) the four
      `BrainState` statuses (`ok`, `no-brain-aide`, `no-mcp-entry`,
      `mcp-drift`); (vii) the verbatim-on-ok /
      fixed-remediation-on-non-ok split, identical across `kind`;
      (viii) the on-demand-only / not-on-boot guidance. Drop
      pre-rework language ("verbatim prose body") and replace with
      the live-section vocabulary. The description must not contain
      the forbidden tokens listed in the parent spec (`vault`,
      `obsidian`, `note` as a synonym for "file", `wikilink`, `hub
      note`, `hub`).
- [x] 4c. In the `aide_brain` case of the
      `CallToolRequestSchema` handler, change `BrainInput.parse(args);
      const result = await brain(root);` to `const parsed =
      BrainInput.parse(args); const result = await brain(root,
      parsed);`. The parsed object carries the optional `kind`
      field; the handler resolves the default. The framework's parse
      step rejects unknown values structurally before the handler
      runs.

